    "extraction_notes": [
      "BAT54SLT1G is a dual series Schottky barrier diode; electrical characteristics are specified for each diode.",
      "The electrical-characteristics table gives maximum forward-voltage limits of 0.24 V at 0.0001 A, 0.32 V at 0.001 A, 0.40 V at 0.01 A, 0.50 V at 0.03 A, and 0.80 V at 0.1 A at TA = 25 degC; typical values are also printed in the table.",
      "The electrical-characteristics table gives maximum reverse leakage of 2 microA at VR = 25 V and maximum total capacitance of 10 pF at VR = 1.0 V and f = 1.0 MHz, all at TA = 25 degC unless otherwise noted.",
      "The plotted forward-current, reverse-leakage, and total-capacitance curves were digitized from Figures 2-4 on p. 3; points are approximate readings of the printed curves and are not interpolated table values.",
      "Reverse recovery time is a maximum 5 ns measured with IF = IR = 10 mA and IR(REC) = 1 mA using the equivalent test circuit in Figure 1.",
      "Reverse breakdown voltage is a minimum 30 V at IR = 10 microA; the 30 V reverse-voltage maximum rating on p. 1 is not treated as a separate breakdown point."
    ],
